<title>USA: FSA qualifies nine muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies nine muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>FSA said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following nine municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Evergreen Sewer Disposal, Mich., $5.8 million of refunding sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--Shakopee, Minn., $2.555 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Newark, N.J., $39.414 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Newark, N.J., $15.102 million GO water utility bonds.</p>
<p>--Newark, N.J., $5 million redevelopment bonds.</p>
<p>--Pohatcong Township, N.J., $1.5 million of general improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Cobleskill-Rich Central School District, N.Y., $9 million GOs.</p>
<p>--New Castle, N.Y., $2.9 million of public improvment bonds.</p>
<p>--Methacton School District, Pa., $9.995 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
